00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.740 align:start position:0%
are you tired of the same old tavern  brawls hearthstone is going to see some  big changes this spring blizzard has  announced new standard and wild modes  for the virtual card game standard mode  is meant for casual friendly games but  you can also play ranked you can use  cards from the Blackrock Mountain Grand  Tournament and League of explorers  expansions but not every card in the  game is available the goal is to keep  each match dynamic and balanced while  making it easier for new players to  learn the ropes wild mode is a different  story it's basically the hearthstone  you're playing now anything can happen  because any card is usable you can keep  earning gold completing quests and  ranking up as much as you want and if  you've already unlocked all nine heroes  you'll get nine extra deck slots which  brings the total to 18 overhauling a  game can be dangerous but it looks like  blizzard found the best of both worlds  with this one there's a full faq on  battlenet if you have any concerns in  the meantime keep playing hearthstone  and keep visiting GameSpot for a full  deck of news and reviews
 

